IMPORT prelude

-- Duties Act 2008 (Western Australia) -- the buyer of a car: what vehicle licence duty must I pay.
--
-- SEAT: the buyer of a vehicle -- the person in whose name the licence is granted, or the transferee, who pays the duty
-- (s 232(1)).
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: Chapter 5, ss 229, 230, 232(1), 236 and 238(1).
--
-- Edition: compilation of the Duties Act 2008 (Act No. 11 of 2008) as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49812.txt (legislation.wa.gov.au mrdoc 49812, retrieved 2026-09-07). The deposit states no
-- compilation number or date; its compilation table ends with the Help to Buy (Commonwealth Powers) Act 2025 Pt. 4 Div. 1 (in
-- operation 19 Dec 2025). No regulation is used. THE FORMULA FOR R IN s 236(2)(b) IS MISSING FROM THE .txt DEPOSIT: only
-- "(rounded to 2 decimal places); where -- DV is the dutiable value" survives. R is therefore an INPUT.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the dutiable value rules for new vehicles (s 237, manufacturer's list price) and specialised vehicles
-- (s 239) -- the value is an input; the seller's and dealer's liability (s 252); exemptions and nominal duty (ss 240-250,
-- and s 250's alternative amount); the "heavy vehicle" definition, which s 228 borrows from the Road Traffic (Vehicles) Act
-- 2012 (a fact).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the seat of the buyer, with the design defaults ruled on
-- 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See
-- NOTES.md.

§ `Duties Act 2008 -- vehicle licence duty`

§§ `ss 229, 230 and 232 -- who pays`

-- s 229: "Duty is imposed on the grant or transfer of a licence for a vehicle." s 230(1): a vehicle is one "required to be
-- licensed under the Vehicles Act, other than a caravan."
-- s 232(1): the duty "is payable by the person in whose name the licence for the vehicle is granted, or the transferee."
@export Must I pay vehicle licence duty on the car I am buying (ss 229, 230, 232)?
GIVEN `it must be licensed under the Vehicles Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle must be licensed under the Road Traffic (Vehicles) Act 2012
      `it is a caravan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is a caravan
      `the licence is granted or transferred to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licence is being granted in your name or transferred to you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I pay vehicle licence duty` IF
        `it must be licensed under the Vehicles Act`
    AND (NOT (`it is a caravan`))
    AND `the licence is granted or transferred to me`

§§ `s 236 -- amount of duty`

-- s 236(1): the amount is worked out under this section "(rounded down to the nearest 5 cents)".
-- s 236(2), not a heavy vehicle: "(a) if the dutiable value of the vehicle does not exceed $25 000 -- 2.75% of the dutiable
-- value; or (b) if the dutiable value of the vehicle exceeds $25 000 but does not exceed $50 000 -- R% of the dutiable value,
-- where R is determined in accordance with the following formula -- [formula absent from the deposit] (rounded to 2 decimal
-- places); ... or (c) if the dutiable value of the vehicle exceeds $50 000 -- 6.5% of the dutiable value."
-- s 236(3), a heavy vehicle: "the lesser of -- (a) 3% of the dutiable value; and (b) $12 000."
-- s 238(1): for a vehicle not under s 237 (a used car, for one), the dutiable value is "the amount for which the vehicle might
-- reasonably be sold, free of encumbrances, in the open market".

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER, `is a heavy vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN, `R` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the vehicle licence duty before rounding` MEANS
    IF `is a heavy vehicle`
    THEN `the lesser of` (`the dutiable value` TIMES 3 DIVIDED BY 100) 12000
    ELSE IF `the dutiable value` AT MOST 25000
         THEN `the dutiable value` TIMES 2.75 DIVIDED BY 100
         ELSE IF `the dutiable value` AT MOST 50000
              THEN `the dutiable value` TIMES `R` DIVIDED BY 100
              ELSE `the dutiable value` TIMES 6.5 DIVIDED BY 100

-- `R` is the percentage under s 236(2)(b), already rounded to 2 decimal places; it is used only when the dutiable value
-- exceeds $25 000 but not $50 000 and the vehicle is not heavy.
@export What vehicle licence duty must I pay on the car I am buying (s 236)?
GIVEN `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER @desc For a used car, what it might reasonably sell for in the open market, in dollars (s 238)
      `is a heavy vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a heavy vehicle
      `R` IS A NUMBER @desc For a value between $25,000 and $50,000, the percentage R from the s 236(2)(b) formula (missing from the deposit)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What vehicle licence duty must I pay` IS
    FLOOR (`the vehicle licence duty before rounding` `the dutiable value` `is a heavy vehicle` `R` TIMES 20) DIVIDED BY 20
